play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.2642,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Patrick Graham"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3186,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2024,"team":"SF","distance":0.3772,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"BAL","distance":0.3968,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2022,"team":"SEA","distance":0.3996,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Dolphins are 1-6 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 181 to 117. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 23rd in EPA per play and the defense 32nd in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits are the lowest pass rate over expected and the 3rd fewest pass rushers in the league.","offense":"The Dolphins offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest pre-snap motion rate in the league. Malik Willis has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Malik Washington, who has drawn 25% of the targets.","defense":"The Dolphins have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 26th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, EPA allowed per rush, only ranks 18th, and it is 32nd in success rate allowed. Chop Robinson has led the way with 4 sacks. Schematically, they have the 3rd fewest pass rushers in the league.","special":"The Dolphins have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 64% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 75% of field goals, which is well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 11% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Malik Willis has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,268 yards. Malik Washington has been the clear top target with 25% of the looks and 329 receiving yards. Ollie Gordon II has handled most of the work in the backfield with 58% of the carries. On defense, Chop Robinson leads the team with 4 sacks and Michael Taaffe has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Bobby Slowik is calling the offense and Sean Duggan is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 49ers under Kyle Shanahan and the 2025 Ravens under Todd Monken. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Raiders under Patrick Graham and the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2025 to 23rd so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 26th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 32nd so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 18% to 64%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}